This src/ directory contains all C++ and CUDA C++ source code for the PSCF 
package.  The subdirectories util, pscf, r1d, prdc, and rp, each contain 
source code for classes and functions defined in a particular C++ 
namespace.  The test subdirectory contains source code for a unit test 
framework.  Subdirectories util/ and test/ are maintained as separate 
github repositories that are installed as submodules of the pscfpp git 
repository when the repository is cloned using the --recursive option.

Subdirectories (with corresponding C++ namespace names in parentheses):

  util - general utilities for scientific computation (Util)
  pscf - classes accessible throughout the PSCF package (Pscf)
  r1d  - real fields, one-dimensional SCFT (Pscf::R1d)
  prdc - periodic systems (Pscf::Prdc)
  rp   - SCFT & PS-FTS with real periodic fields, CPU & GPU (Pscf::Rp)
  test - unit testing framework (base classes)

  Program-level directories:
  Directories r1d and rp are "program level" directories, which each 
  contain files that generate one or more executables.  By convention, 
  source files in one program-level directory may never include files 
  from a different program-level directory.

  Dependencies among directories:
  Names of classes and other entitites defined in files located in the 
  util and pscf directories may be used anywhere in the PSCF package. 
  Names defined in the prdc directory are used in the rp program-level 
  directory but not in the r1d directory.

Files (maintained in the git repository):

  setopts  - script for managing compile-time options
  makefile - main makefile for in-source compilation (build in src)
  programs.mod - doxygen page for program command-line interfaces
  CONTENTS - this file

Files (installed by the configure script):

  config.mk - main configuration file (editable makefile fragment)

